      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #6, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ Bif_F12_CIRCLE (○) was the only scalar function missing its
      ⍝ eval_AXB() override, so a dyadic axis specification fell through
      ⍝ to Function::phrase_error() -- VALENCE ERROR -- even though every
      ⍝ dyadic scalar function is required to accept an axis (apl2lrm.txt
      ⍝ Figure 7 p.45, Figure 9 p.51). Added the same eval_AXB() every
      ⍝ other scalar function class already has.
      ⍝
