      ⍝ Bugs28 #47 regression: A○B with a genuinely complex A (non-zero
      ⍝ imaginary part, e.g. 1J1) silently used only A's real part
      ⍝ instead of raising DOMAIN ERROR -- RealCell.cc/ComplexCell.cc's
      ⍝ bif_circle_fun() checked A->is_near_int() for validity, and
      ⍝ ComplexCell::is_near_int() used to return true whenever BOTH
      ⍝ parts were independently near-integral (1J1 qualified), then
      ⍝ get_checked_near_int() silently returned just the real part.
      ⍝ Already fixed as a side effect of the Bugs28 #32 fix to
      ⍝ ComplexCell::is_near_int()/is_near_int64_t(), which now also
      ⍝ requires the imaginary part be ≈0 -- kept here as its own
      ⍝ regression test since #32's fix was for a different symptom
      ⍝ (parse-time constant folding / a stack overflow).
      ⍝
