      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #85): 4○, ¯4○, 8○, ¯8○ and 0○ computed
      ⍝ sqrt(1±b²) (or sqrt(b²-1)) directly, so b*b overflowed to +∞ for
      ⍝ any |b| above roughly 1.34E154 even though the true result
      ⍝ (≈|b|) is perfectly finite -- the interpreter's own is_finite()
      ⍝ safety net then turned that overflow into a spurious DOMAIN
      ⍝ ERROR. 4○/8○/¯8○ now use hypot(1.0, b), and ¯4○/0○ use
      ⍝ |b|×sqrt(1-1÷b²), neither of which needs to square b directly.
      ⍝
