      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #12): the r2127 fix above's
      ⍝ 8○ shortcut (hypot(1.0, b.real())) always builds a POSITIVE-
      ⍝ imaginary root, but the sign selection below it (unchanged,
      ⍝ written for the general complex_sqrt() path) consulted the
      ⍝ actual, tiny, no-longer-reflected-in-root b.imag() -- flipping
      ⍝ the sign for a near-real b whose tiny imaginary part shares its
      ⍝ real part's sign, disagreeing with both the exactly-real
      ⍝ neighbour and the just-outside-band general-path neighbour.
