      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #14): ¯7○'s (arctanh) r2127
      ⍝ near-zero-imaginary shortcut discarded b.imag() unconditionally,
      ⍝ but d(atanh)/dx = 1/(1-x²) blows up as b.real() approaches ±1,
      ⍝ so even a tiny imaginary part can contribute non-negligibly once
      ⍝ amplified -- ¯7○z must agree with its own definition
      ⍝ 0.5×((⍟1+z)-(⍟1-z)) for such a z.
      ⍝
